<article class="env-lemma" id="0G4K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G4K">Lemma <span data-tag="0G4K">48.30.2</span>.</a> The result of Lemma <a href="/tag/0G2H" data-tag="0G2H">48.30.1</a> holds even for $L \in D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, if $(K_ n)$ is a Deligne system then there exists a $b \in \mathbf{Z}$ such that $H^ i(K_ n) = 0$ for $i > b$. Then $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K_ n, L) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K_ n, \tau _{\leq b}L)$ and $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K, L) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K, \tau _{\leq b}L)$. Hence using the result of the lemma for $\tau _{\leq b}L$ we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>